# MDX roadmap (approved direction)

## Status

- All guides are hand-written TSX today; **no MDX dependencies installed**
- Safe to add MDX incrementally; static `app/guides/<slug>/page.tsx` routes always beat a future `[slug]` dynamic route

## Preferred approach when user asks for MDX

1. Add `content/guides/<slug>.mdx` with frontmatter (`title`, `description`, flags)
2. New articles only first; thin `page.tsx` or later `app/guides/[slug]` for MDX-only slugs
3. Keep `GuideArticleShell` + conversion blocks in TSX initially; MDX for prose body
4. Wrappers: `TipBox` / `InfoBox` → `Callout`; `AffiliateBlock` → `InlineAffiliate`
5. Stack option: `next-mdx-remote/rsc` + `gray-matter` (content folder outside `app/`)

## Do not without explicit approval

- Replace all 37 existing guide pages at once
- Change global UI or conversion placement site-wide
- Auto-publish hub cards without updating `lib/tourist-guides.ts` and `app/sitemap.ts`

## Tailwind

If MDX uses raw classes in markdown, add `./content/**/*.{md,mdx}` to `tailwind.config.ts` `content` array.
